; The quadruped's key poses and cycles - its front legs are its arm bones, its hind legs its leg bones, and every
; bone a pose leaves out is held straight.

[; standing square on all fours, head up
 [Pose Stance [[Turns [[Head [[Lean -2.8648]]]]]]]

 ; gathered to spring - legs splayed out fore and aft so the body sinks low, head drawn back
 [Pose Coil
  [[Turns
    [[Torso [[Lean 4.5837]]]
     [Head [[Lean -14.3239]]]
     [ArmLeft [[Swing 20.0535]]]
     [ArmRight [[Swing 20.0535]]]
     [LegLeft [[Swing -20.0535]]]
     [LegRight [[Swing -20.0535]]]]]]]

 ; springing - stretched out long, forelegs reaching, hind legs thrown back, head thrust ahead
 [Pose Leap
  [[Turns
    [[Torso [[Lean -4.5837]]]
     [Head [[Lean 11.4592]]]
     [ArmLeft [[Swing 42.9718]]]
     [ArmRight [[Swing 34.3775]]]
     [LegLeft [[Swing -37.2423]]]
     [LegRight [[Swing -31.5127]]]]]]]

 ; the blow - the head and shoulders driven down into the foe, a foreleg raking through it
 [Pose Bite
